<section class="ref-group"><h2>Sieges <span class="n">4</span></h2><ul class="enc-list"><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/alexanders-siege-of-gaza"><span class="enc-name">Alexander's siege of Gaza</span><span class="enc-type">Siege</span><span class="enc-snip">Alexander's siege of Gaza was a siege by the army of Alexander the Great in 332 BCE, following the capture of Tyre, as he advanced towards Egypt.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/siege-of-acre-1189-1191"><span class="enc-name">Siege of Acre (1189–1191)</span><span class="enc-type">Siege</span><span class="enc-snip">The Siege of Acre (1189–1191) was a long siege of the port city of Acre during the Third Crusade.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/siege-of-paris-885-886"><span class="enc-name">Siege of Paris (885–886)</span><span class="enc-type">Siege</span><span class="enc-snip">The Siege of Paris (885–886) was a siege of Paris by a large Viking army.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/siege-of-urshu"><span class="enc-name">Siege of Urshu</span><span class="enc-type">Siege</span><span class="enc-snip">The Siege of Urshu was a siege by the Hittites of the city of Urshu in northern Syria, recorded in a Hittite text.</span></a></li></ul></section>
<section class="ref-group"><h2>Wars &amp; campaigns <span class="n">34</span></h2><ul class="enc-list"><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/anglo-dutch-wars"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/anglo-dutch-wars.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Anglo-Dutch Wars</span><span class="enc-type">War</span><span class="enc-snip">The Anglo-Dutch Wars were a series of naval wars fought between England and the Dutch Republic in the seventeenth and eighteenth centuries.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/arab-khazar-wars"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/arab-khazar-wars.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Arab–Khazar wars</span><span class="enc-type">War</span><span class="enc-snip">The Arab–Khazar wars were a series of conflicts in the seventh and eighth centuries between the Khazar Khaganate and the Umayyad and early Abbasid caliphates over…</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/chu-han-contention"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/chu-han-contention.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Chu–Han Contention</span><span class="enc-type">War</span><span class="enc-snip">The Chu-Han Contention was the civil war that followed the collapse of the Qin dynasty in the late third century BCE, fought between Xiang Yu of Chu and Liu Bang of Han.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/cisplatine-war"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/cisplatine-war.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Cisplatine War</span><span class="enc-type">War</span><span class="enc-snip">The Cisplatine War was fought from 1825 to 1828 between the Brazilian Empire and the United Provinces of the Río de la Plata over the Cisplatine Province, present-day…</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/crusade"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/crusade.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Crusade</span><span class="enc-type">War</span><span class="enc-snip">A crusade was a war sanctioned by the papacy, typically against Muslims or other perceived enemies of the Church, in which participants received spiritual privileges.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/crusades"><span class="enc-name">Crusades</span><span class="enc-type">War</span><span class="enc-snip">The Crusades were a series of religious wars launched by Latin Christians from the late eleventh century, chiefly to capture and hold Jerusalem and the Holy Land.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/dano-swedish-wars"><span class="enc-name">Dano-Swedish wars</span><span class="enc-type">War</span><span class="enc-snip">The Dano-Swedish wars were a long series of conflicts between Denmark-Norway and Sweden for control of Scandinavia and the Baltic.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/dutch-revolt"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/dutch-revolt.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Dutch Revolt</span><span class="enc-type">Revolt · War</span><span class="enc-snip">The Dutch Revolt was the uprising of the Netherlands against Spanish Habsburg rule that began in the 1560s and led to the independence of the Dutch Republic.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/first-italo-ethiopian-war"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/first-italo-ethiopian-war.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">First Italo-Ethiopian War</span><span class="enc-type">War</span><span class="enc-snip">The First Italo-Ethiopian War was fought in 1895–1896 between Italy and the Ethiopian Empire under Menelik II.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/first-world-war"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/first-world-war.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">First World War</span><span class="enc-type">War</span><span class="enc-snip">The First World War (1914–1918) was a global conflict between the Allied Powers, including Britain, France and Russia, and the Central Powers, including Germany…</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/flower-wars"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/flower-wars.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Flower Wars</span><span class="enc-type">War</span><span class="enc-snip">The Flower Wars were ritualised conflicts fought by the Aztec Empire with neighbouring states such as Tlaxcala.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/franco-prussian-war"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/franco-prussian-war.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Franco-Prussian War</span><span class="enc-type">War</span><span class="enc-snip">The Franco-Prussian War of 1870–1871 was fought between France and a German coalition led by Prussia.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/french-revolutionary-wars"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/french-revolutionary-wars.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">French Revolutionary Wars</span><span class="enc-type">War</span><span class="enc-snip">The French Revolutionary Wars (1792–1802) were fought between revolutionary France and coalitions of European powers.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/french-sahelian-mission"><span class="enc-name">French Sahelian Mission</span><span class="enc-type">Campaign</span><span class="enc-snip">The French Sahelian Mission refers to the French military advance into the central Sahel in the early twentieth century.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/french-wars-of-religion"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/french-wars-of-religion.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">French Wars of Religion</span><span class="enc-type">War</span><span class="enc-snip">The French Wars of Religion were a series of civil wars between Catholics and Protestants (Huguenots) in France in the second half of the sixteenth century.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/goguryeo-sui-war"><span class="enc-name">Goguryeo–Sui War</span><span class="enc-type">War</span><span class="enc-snip">The Goguryeo–Sui War was a series of failed invasions of the Korean kingdom of Goguryeo by the Sui dynasty in the early seventh century.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/greco-persian-wars"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/greco-persian-wars.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Greco-Persian Wars</span><span class="enc-type">War</span><span class="enc-snip">The Greco-Persian Wars were a series of conflicts in the fifth century BCE between the Achaemenid Empire and Greek city-states, including Athens and Sparta.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/han-campaigns-against-the-xiongnu-120s-110s-bce"><span class="enc-name">Han campaigns against the Xiongnu (120s–110s BCE)</span><span class="enc-type">Campaign</span><span class="enc-snip">The Han campaigns against the Xiongnu of the 120s and 110s BCE were a series of large offensives launched by the Han Dynasty under Emperor Wu into the steppe.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/italian-wars"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/italian-wars.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Italian Wars</span><span class="enc-type">War</span><span class="enc-snip">The Italian Wars were a series of conflicts between 1494 and 1559 fought mainly between France and Spain, along with other powers, for control of Italy.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/jinchuan-campaigns"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/jinchuan-campaigns.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Jinchuan campaigns</span><span class="enc-type">Campaign</span><span class="enc-snip">The Jinchuan campaigns were military expeditions of the Qing Empire in the eighteenth century against the Jinchuan chieftaincies in the mountains of western Sichuan.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/kalebs-yemen-campaign"><span class="enc-name">Kaleb's Yemen campaign</span><span class="enc-type">Campaign</span><span class="enc-snip">Kaleb's Yemen campaign was the Aksumite military expedition to South Arabia in the sixth century CE under King Kaleb.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/livonian-war"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/livonian-war.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Livonian War</span><span class="enc-type">War</span><span class="enc-snip">The Livonian War was a conflict from 1558 to 1583 over control of Livonia, fought by Russia under Ivan IV against Poland-Lithuania, Sweden and Denmark.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/march-across-the-belts"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/march-across-the-belts.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">March across the Belts</span><span class="enc-type">Campaign</span><span class="enc-snip">The March across the Belts was a campaign in 1658 in which King Charles X Gustav of Sweden led his army across the frozen straits of Denmark.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/mfecane"><img class="enc-thumb"